{"issue":{"title":"Add a --shout option to greet and document it in docs/","problem":"bin/greet.js has no --shout option. It takes the first argument that does not start with '--' as the name and silently drops every '--' argument, so `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints the normal `Hello, Ada!` with no error. src/greet.js only exports `greeting(name)`, which returns `Hello, <name>!`. docs/index.md, which .github/workflows/pages.yml publishes to the docs site on every push to main, documents only `node bin/greet.js <name>`. test/greet.test.js has no test for a shouted greeting.","reason":"Support staff want a louder greeting for the lobby screen, and they want a docs page they can send people to. Because the CLI drops unknown flags today, someone who tries --shout gets the normal greeting and no hint that the flag does nothing.","outcome":"`greet --shout <name>` prints the greeting in upper case, and plain `greet <name>` works as before. docs/index.md documents --shout, so the docs site shows it after the next push to main publishes docs/.","expect":["Running `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` exits 0 and writes exactly `HELLO, ADA!\\n` to stdout.","Running `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` (flag after the name) exits 0 and writes exactly `HELLO, ADA!\\n` to stdout.","Running `node bin/greet.js Ada` without the flag still exits 0 and writes exactly `Hello, Ada!\\n` to stdout.","Running `node bin/greet.js --shout` with no name exits with status 2, writes a usage message to stderr and writes nothing to stdout.","docs/index.md documents the `--shout` option, with an example command that uses it and the upper-case output it produces (for example `HELLO, <NAME>!`).","`npm test` passes, and test/greet.test.js contains at least one test that runs the CLI with `--shout` and checks the upper-case output."],"proofs":[{"line":"Running `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` exits 0 and writes exactly `HELLO, ADA!\\n` to stdout.","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js --shout Ada | od -c; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"  # expect H E L L O ,   A D A ! \\n and exit=0"},{"line":"Running `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` (flag after the name) exits 0 and writes exactly `HELLO, ADA!\\n` to stdout.","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js Ada --shout | od -c; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"  # expect HELLO, ADA!\\n and exit=0"},{"line":"Running `node bin/greet.js Ada` without the flag still exits 0 and writes exactly `Hello, Ada!\\n` to stdout.","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js Ada | od -c; echo \"exit=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"  # expect Hello, Ada!\\n and exit=0"},{"line":"Running `node bin/greet.js --shout` with no name exits with status 2, writes a usage message to stderr and writes nothing to stdout.","proof":"run","how":"node bin/greet.js --shout >out.txt 2>err.txt; echo \"exit=$?\"; wc -c out.txt; cat err.txt  # expect exit=2, out.txt 0 bytes, a usage line in err.txt"},{"line":"docs/index.md documents the `--shout` option, with an example command that uses it and the upper-case output it produces (for example `HELLO, <NAME>!`).","proof":"read","how":"Read docs/index.md at the PR head. It must mention `--shout`, show a command that uses it, and show the upper-case output."},{"line":"`npm test` passes, and test/greet.test.js contains at least one test that runs the CLI with `--shout` and checks the upper-case output.","proof":"run","how":"npm test (expect `# fail 0`), then: grep -n -- '--shout' test/greet.test.js (expect a test that runs bin/greet.js with --shout and asserts upper-case output)"}],"non_goals":["Publishing or deploying the docs site, or checking the live page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/. The existing pages workflow publishes docs/ after merge to main; this PR only has to change docs/index.md.","Changing .github/workflows/pages.yml.","Adding other options (such as a short alias like -s, custom greetings or other languages), or rejecting unknown flags in general.","Publishing a release or bumping the package version."],"assumptions":["'Louder' means the whole greeting line in upper case, so `Hello, Ada!` becomes `HELLO, ADA!`. The name is upper-cased too and the punctuation stays the same; no extra exclamation marks are added.","The flag works anywhere in the arguments (before or after the name), to match how bin/greet.js already reads arguments.","`--shout` with no name is a usage error, the same as running with no arguments today (exit 2, usage on stderr). The usage text may be updated to mention --shout.","The request's 'make sure it shows up on the published docs site' is met in the PR by documenting --shout in docs/index.md, because the existing pages workflow publishes docs/ on every push to main.","Whether the shouting is done in src/greet.js (for example a new option or export) or only in bin/greet.js is the builder's choice; the request doesn't name a function."]}}